# Storefront nav — absolute collection links only

Mega menus, top nav, and Getting started hand-offs must **never** use Shopify **search** URLs (`/search?q=…`) or fuzzy title matching for product shelves.

## Required pattern

| Layer | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| **ERP** | Canonical taxonomy (`department`, `grade`, `subline`, `product_line`, `type`, …) |
| **Tag resolver** | Absolute storefront tags (`mk:*`, `misc:*`, `ts:*`) from ERP columns — not description keyword search in Liquid |
| **Shopify Admin** | Smart collection: product tag **equals** each shelf tag (OR when catalog says so) |
| **Theme / nav** | **`/collections/{handle}`** only, or T&S pre-filter URLs documented in `tools-supplies-classification.md` (`/collections/paints?ovs_paint_app=…`) |

## Forbidden in nav Liquid

- `/search?q=…`
- `/collections/all?…` as a shelf substitute
- Guessing handles that are not in a shelf catalog (`ModelKitShelfCatalog`, `MiscShelfCatalog`, `WorkshopShelfCatalog`)

## Adding a new mega menu link

1. Classify SKUs in ERP (taxonomy derivation / verification).
2. Add tag + shelf row to the appropriate catalog PHP class.
3. Run shelf provisioning artisan command + tag push to Shopify.
4. Wire `/collections/{handle}` in the mega menu snippet.
5. Browser QA: collection count matches ERP expectation — not “search looks close enough”.

